WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
Read the rule before the price.
Live Panta response · resolution wording and indicative values

2
00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:13.000
Keep a checkpoint before refreshing.
Saved locally in this browser · no account or wallet required

3
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:15.000
Refresh the source.
Direct Panta request · waiting state captured as it happened

4
00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:22.000
This response omits rules and prices.
The application preserves missing fields instead of inventing them

5
00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:30.000
Eight tracked fields changed.
The earlier wording remains in the checkpoint; the new capture says “Not supplied”

6
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:40.000
Read a real DBC pool on Solana mainnet.
Solami supplies account data; Sourcebrief decodes Meteora configuration

7
00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:47.000
Keep the slot and capture time.
A dated checkpoint makes the next review comparable

8
00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:56.000
A threshold is not completed migration.
Configured liquidity shares are not verified destination balances

9
00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:03.000
Inspect the curve and fee terms.
The interface distinguishes pool configuration from execution conditions

10
00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:08.000
Enter a 0.05 SOL scenario.
No wallet, signature, transaction simulation or order

11
00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:11.000
Capture fresh accounts, then calculate.
The calculation uses the official Meteora SDK

12
00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:24.000
A mathematical result, not an executed trade.
0.05 SOL input · 0.001 SOL SDK fee · source slot 455038532

13
00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:32.000
Compare facts, not only timestamps.
No tracked facts changed here; that does not prove no on-chain activity

14
00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:42.000
Trace the account context and source hashes.
The capture records provider, mainnet, commitment, slot and configuration

15
00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:47.000
Export the dated record as JSON.
The application confirms export with source timing and limitations

16
00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:52.000
Take the same evidence as Markdown.
A portable brief preserves the source context for a reviewer

17
00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:55.000
Read a second pool with a transfer hook.
Another real Solami request · loading state preserved

18
00:01:55.000 --> 00:02:04.000
Inspect the configuration. Keep its limits.
An external transfer hook changes what can be asserted about execution

19
00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:12.000
Unsupported execution stays unsupported.
The application returns “Estimate unavailable” instead of a plausible number

20
00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:20.000
Sourcebrief: evidence you can inspect.
